Dear Hiring Team,

\vspace{0.8em}

I am a Data Science graduate student at the University of Maryland, currently interning as an ML Engineer at Nokia, where I build retrieval infrastructure for large-scale RAG systems. My primary project is a Knowledge Layer that unifies vector search (OpenSearch), relational metadata (PostgreSQL), and graph traversal (Neo4j) to support semantic querying over large corpora of technical documentation. Alongside this, I designed a Multimodal RAG pipeline using Jina Embeddings V4 and OpenAI CLIP that enables natural-language querying over figures and tables.

\vspace{1em}

Before Nokia, I spent two and a half years as a Data Scientist in Maruti Suzuki's R\&D division. I built and deployed an LSTM-based battery health prediction system on vehicle telematics data, achieving 98\% field-validated accuracy across 100K+ connected vehicles. The system reduced roadside failures and warranty claims at scale, and the underlying method was granted a patent (No.~202411040338). I also audited a training pipeline that was consuming \$4{,}000 per month in GPU compute, identified the bottlenecks, and migrated the workloads to multi-core CPU execution with no loss in model accuracy.

\vspace{1em}

Outside of industry work, I co-authored a paper in \textit{Nature Scientific Reports} on ML applied to high-dimensional genomic data for stress biomarker identification in aquaculture, and hold a granted patent for the battery prediction system deployed in production across Maruti Suzuki's connected vehicle fleet.

\vspace{1em}

I would love a chance to work at {{.Company}} because of the opportunity to apply ML to a domain where the feedback loops are fast and impactful. Looking forward to discussing how my background fits what your team is building.

